    <!-- Terms and Conditions -->
    <string name="title_terms_conditions">📜 Terms and Conditions of Use</string>
    <string name="terms_body">By using FactorEscalaTop 2.4, you formally accept the following terms and conditions:\n\n
        <b>Geographic Scope:</b> The application is designed and calibrated exclusively for the reference systems and cartographic grid of Bolivia.\n\n
        <b>Technical Support Tool:</b> The data provided is for guidance only and does not replace the procedures, technical controls, or professional equipment required for official or legal surveys.\n\n
        <b>Reference Systems:</b> The app utilizes official <b>MGBol08</b> models and the global <b>EGM2008</b> standard for geodetic precision.\n\n
        <b>Connectivity and APIs:</b> "Online Height" and "Weather" functions depend on third-party services (Open-Meteo, Esri). The availability of these external services depends on their own providers.\n\n
        <b>User Responsibility:</b> It is the professional\'s exclusive obligation to verify, validate, and certify all calculations before their application in formal projects.\n\n
        <b>Limit of Liability:</b> The developer assumes no responsibility for damages derived from the use or reliance on the application\'s calculations.\n\n
        <b>Regulatory Compliance:</b> The user agrees to use the tool in accordance with Law 164 and current regulations in the Plurinational State of Bolivia.</string>

    <string name="title_privacy_policy">🔒 Privacy Policy</string>
    <string name="privacy_body">In compliance with Google Play guidelines for data protection, this policy details how information is managed:\n\n
        <b>Location Usage (GPS):</b> The application processes real-time geolocation data to execute geodetic calculations and project maps. Data is processed locally and may be used in the background to maintain session pin persistence.\n\n
        <b>Local Storage and Export:</b> Points and records are stored exclusively in the device\'s internal memory. Exported files (TXT/JSON) are the user\'s responsibility.\n\n
        <b>Third-Party Services:</b> We use Google Play Services for maps, Open-Meteo API for weather and elevation data, and ArcGIS (Esri) for satellite layers.\n\n
        <b>Security:</b> No personal data is collected or sold to external developer servers.</string>

