    <string name="title_quick_guide">📖 Quick User Guide</string>

    <string name="guide_section_gen_title">1. General Concepts</string>
    <string name="guide_section_gen_body">FactorEscalaTop 2.4 is a comprehensive topographic suite for calculating correction factors (k, ha, K), GNSS data management, and map measurements, specifically calibrated for Bolivia.</string>

    <string name="guide_section_calc_title">2. Calculation Modes</string>
    <string name="guide_section_calc_body"><b>Automatic:</b> Obtains real-time data from GPS.\n<b>Manual:</b> Allows simulating scenarios by entering coordinates from blueprints or projects.</string>

    <string name="guide_section_map_title">3. Navigation and Map</string>
    <string name="guide_section_map_body"><b>Orange Crosshair:</b> Central target.\n<b>Search (Magnifier):</b> Navigate to exact coordinates.\n<b>Interactive Points:</b> Tap a point\'s name to see its technical sheet.\n<b>Measurement:</b> Use the <b>Light Blue</b> button for areas and <b>Red</b> for distances.</string>

    <string name="guide_section_alt_title">4. Altitude and DEM Models</string>
    <string name="guide_section_alt_body"><b>Device GPS:</b> Ellipsoidal height from the mobile.\n<b>Online Height:</b> Obtains the elevation (MSL) via Open-Meteo API (Copernicus DEM) with EGM2008 correction.</string>

    <string name="guide_section_drone_title">5. Flight Assistant</string>
    <string name="guide_section_drone_body">Analyzes drone safety via traffic light (Green to Red). Tap the <b>SATELLITES</b> section for a detailed constellation diagnosis and signal strength.</string>

    <string name="guide_section_data_title">6. Data Management</string>
    <string name="guide_section_data_body">Export your surveys in <b>TXT</b> for human reports or <b>JSON</b> for direct integration with GIS/CAD software from the RECORDS tab.</string>

